{"name":"Snakebite","hex":"#bb4444","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snakebite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bite of a snake.","A cocktail made with equal parts lager and hard cider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snakebite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snakebite","blocks":[{"text":"A snakebite is an injury caused by the bite of a snake. Most snake species are non-venomous, but bites from venomous snakes may result in envenomation, in which venom is injected into the victim. A common sign of a bite from a venomous snake is the presence of two puncture wounds from the animal's fangs. Envenomation may cause redness, swelling, and severe pain around the bite, which may take up to an hour to develop. Vomiting, blurred vision, tingling of the limbs, and sweating may result. Most bites are on the hands, arms, or legs. Fear following a bite is common with symptoms of a racing heart and feeling faint. The venom may cause bleeding, kidney failure, a severe allergic reaction, tissue death around the bite, or breathing problems. Bites may result in the loss of a limb or other chronic problems or even death."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Cobra_bite_in_Thailand_%28image%2C_2023%29.jpg/330px-Cobra_bite_in_Thailand_%28image%2C_2023%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakebite"},{"title":"Snakebite (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Snakebite is the first official release by the British rock band Whitesnake. The original EP initially featured only four tracks and was released primarily in the UK in June 1978."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/01/SnakebiteEP.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakebite_(EP)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Snake_bite_symptoms.png/500px-Snake_bite_symptoms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Snake_bite_symptoms.png/1280px-Snake_bite_symptoms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Snake_bite_symptoms.png/500px-Snake_bite_symptoms.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The most common symptoms of any kind of snake envenomation.[20][21][22] However, there is vast variation in symptoms between bites from different types of snakes.[20]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnake_bite_symptoms.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Tissue_necrosis_following_bite_from_Bothrops_asper_PLoS_Medicine.jpg/500px-Tissue_necrosis_following_bite_from_Bothrops_asper_PLoS_Medicine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Tissue_necrosis_following_bite_from_Bothrops_asper_PLoS_Medicine.jpg/500px-Tissue_necrosis_following_bite_from_Bothrops_asper_PLoS_Medicine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Severe tissue necrosis following Bothrops asper envenomation that required amputation above the knee. The person was an 11-year-old boy, bitten two weeks earlier in Ecuador, but treated only with antibiotics.[28]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATissue_necrosis_following_bite_from_Bothrops_asper_PLoS_Medicine.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/RodriguezParkHoustonSnakes.JPG/500px-RodriguezParkHoustonSnakes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/RodriguezParkHoustonSnakes.JPG/1280px-RodriguezParkHoustonSnakes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa